        dtDes: 'Located in bussines district.',
        introduction: 'Introduction',
        I1Text: 'With the aim to standardize the damage evaluation process, we have prepared a catalogue of damage costs to unify and standardize the processes of inspection, processing and charging for the vehicle damages at HERTZ offices.',
        I2Text: 'The damage catalogue is designed to help you locate and identify the proportion of vehicle damages easily. It also serves as a reminder for Rent-a-Car users to choose to buy additional covers when booking/taking over a vehicle. Its a manual in which HERTZ employees and clients can find different examples of damage and appropriate amounts for charging.',
        I3Text: 'The catalogue contains an estimate of costs incurred by a particular damage and may include part of the cost calculated according to the number of days needed to repair the vehicle, including possible waiting for the delivery of spare parts.',
        I4Text: 'The damage catalogue describes many kinds of damage that were not caused by ordinary or conventional use of the vehicle. Only one damage can be charged for one vehicle element (e.g. if there is moredamage to one element, only the largest/most expensive damage is charged for). There is also a possibility of charging for additional costs such as administrative costs, towing or transport costs.',
        I5Text: 'An office that rented a vehicle is obliged to explain the way to act in case of the damage or technical malfunction of the vehicle to the client in detail.',
        I6Text: 'After determining the proportion of damage, only Autotechnica Fleet Services d.o.o. has the right to decide when the damage to the vehicle will be repaired. The vehiclecan be rented again if the vehicle does not need necessary repairs and if it is the correct technical condition.',
        I7Text: 'If there is an adequate cover for the type of damage the client has done to the vehicle as well as the necessary documentation about the incident involving damage, the client will not be charged for the damage.',
        I8Text: 'In case that the damage to the vehicle is not covered by any additional cover, it must be charged according to the pre-defined rates and the category of the rented vehicle from the deposit of funds reserved on the credit card at the takeover of the vehicle, or at the request of the client, by another means of payment up to the maximum amount of the franchise. Additionally, an administrative fee for processing a damage incident is charged according to the valid price list. Charges are made upon returning the rented vehicle.',
        vehicleInstructions: 'In the case of vehicle theft, car burglary, vandalism or damage to a parked vehicle call (+385) 192 for the police immediately and contact Hertz office for further instructions.',
        I9Text: 'The client is obliged to present all the documents handed to him/her by the police or other person (police report, alcotest record, filled European accident statement) and fill in the damage report at the vehicle return office.',
        I10Text: 'Autotechnica Fleet Services d.o.o. reserves the right to charge the entire amount of the damage incurred if the client acted contrary to the law regulations of the Republic of Croatia or did not respect the prescribed procedures for reporting a damage event.',
        I11Text: 'Damage that resulted due to client negligence (burnt clutch, damage to the inside of the vehicle, driving with a punctured tyre/damaged wheel, etc.) will be charged in full, regardless of the purchase of additional covers.',
        I12Text: 'How to act in case of a minor traffic accident and/or damage to the vehicle, theft, attempted theft of the vehicle and or in case of vehicle burglary, and vandalism?',
        I13Text: 'In case of an accident and/or damage to the vehicle, the client must immediately call the police number (+385) 192 and fill in the European accident statement if another vehicle was involved in the car accident. If the rented vehicle is not in the driving condition, please contact Hertz office. Upon returning the rented vehicle, agents/referents are required to request the alcotest record given to the client by the police as well as all the other relevant documentation connected to the incident.',
        I14Text: 'In the case of vehicle theft, car burglary, vandalism or damage to a parked vehicle call (+385) 192 for the police immediately and contact Hertz office for further instructions.',
        I15Text: 'The agent at the office is obliged to make minimum 3 photographs of each damage and together with the complete documentation (police record, statement by the driver on the damage incident, the alcotest, etc.) to enter them into the system. Likewise, if the vehicle is damaged, the agent is required to notify the Hertz technical department by mail/call to order the vehicle for service/body repairs.',
        dmgEvaluator: 'Damage evaluator',
        E1Text: 'Each agent will use a "tool"- evaluator for surface damage on the vehicle when inspecting the damage to the vehicle at the office. Damage evaluator is a tool by which an agent and a client can more easily detect (measure) the size of the damage and determine whether the damage is subject to charge or can be tolerated since minor damage to car paint up to 1 cm (e.g., made by little stones) is not subject to charging.',
        E2Text: 'There are two circles on the damage evaluator and a meter in centimetres to measure the size of the damage on the vehicle and to easily determine the proportion of the damage in the photographs. As shown on the damage measurement evaluator itself, any damage is measurable and detailed in terms of damages that are subject to charging.',
        DefOdDmg: 'Damage definitions',
        Scratch: 'Scratch',
        ScratchPara: 'Scratches are physical damage to surfaces caused by sharp/pointed objects and are most often seen as minor damage. Damages by scratches are determined by their length and width (e.g. 6 x 1.5 cm).',
        Dent: 'Dent',
        DentPara: 'A dent is any convex (bulged or protruded) or concave (dented) damage to the vehicle. Dents on the plastic parts of the vehicle are not subject to repair and such parts of the vehicle are in most cases replaced by new original parts.',
        BCMNas: 'Broken / Cracked / Missing',
        BCMNasPara: 'A dent is any convex (bulgedor protruded) or concave(dented) damage to the vehicle. Dents on the plastic parts of the vehicle are not subject to repair and such parts of the vehicle are in most cases replaced by new original parts.',
        Rip: 'Rip',
        RipPara: 'Rip is caused by external influences, overloads, or negligent handling of sharp objects. This category includes carpet damage,damaged seat uphalstery and interior trim.',
        RipPara2: 'U ovu kategoriju ubrajamo oštećenja tepiha, presvlaka sjedala i unutarnjih obloga vozila.',
        Dirt: 'Dirt',
        DirtPara: 'This category refers to the excessive dirtiness of the vehicle, especially the inside of the boot or/and the interior of the vehicle. Dirt comes from negligence in the interior of the vehicle. Visible stains that cannot be removed - are considered a damage. The dirt that cannot be removed by conventional cleaning is considered a damage.',
        Mal: 'Malfunction',
